  "details": "The current Parameter Behavior system is fairly powerful, however it would save me a lot of code duplication and make it easier to maintain a large number of expressions If I could re-use the result of already evaluated expressions.\n\nFor instance, if I have an expression like:\n\n `MouthCornerPullRight * 0.8 + MouthCornerSlantRight * 0.2` \n\nthat runs a blendhshape or parameter `MouthSmileRight`, then I could re-use that calculation in another expression like this:\n\n`MouthSmileRight - MouthFrownRight` and output that to a parameter or shape `SmileFrownRight`. \n\nIdeally either the animator parameter name or blendshape name could be used as the token to reference its value in subsequent expressions.",
